(# Frontier Model SLM: Market Entry Executive Brief) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Executive Thesis) Tj
T*
(The Frontier Model SLM should not enter the market by chasing the largest possible buyer first.) Tj
T*
(It should enter through the buyer profile that best supports rapid proof, high-value outcomes) Tj
T*
(data, repeatable GTM learning, and later expansion into larger and more complex markets.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(That starting profile is **closed-loop talent transformation / placement intermediaries**.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These buyers are not the largest long-run market. But they are the strongest first market) Tj
T*
(because they sit at the intersection of strategic workforce planning pain, observable routing) Tj
T*
(and placement outcomes, and enough operational control to create a usable feedback loop. That) Tj
T*
(makes them the best environment for proving the product and improving the model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The recommended GTM sequence is:) Tj
T*
(1. Closed-loop talent transformation / placement intermediaries) Tj
T*
(2. Employer-connected mission / workforce intermediaries) Tj
T*
(3. Community college apprenticeship / pathway programs) Tj
T*
(4. Large employers with strategic workforce planning pain) Tj
T*
(5. Higher-ed institutions with co-op / externship outcome closure) Tj
T*
(6. State workforce agencies / systems) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Why This Matters) Tj
T*
(The first buyer profile does a different job than later ones. It must:) Tj
T*
(- prove the Frontier Model SLM works in real planning environments) Tj
T*
(- generate outcomes data that improves the model) Tj
T*
(- create a repeatable GTM motion) Tj
T*
(- produce references and evidence strong enough to support larger sales later) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If the product enters through a buyer profile that is too slow, too bespoke, too politically) Tj
T*
(constrained, or too weak on outcomes visibility, it may miss the chance to build compounding) Tj
T*
(proof. That is why large employers and state systems, while strategically important, should not) Tj
T*
(be first.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Core Recommendation) Tj
T*
(### Start with: Closed-loop talent transformation / placement intermediaries) Tj
T*
(Why this profile wins:) Tj
T*
(- best combination of planning pain and direct SLM fit) Tj
T*
(- strong speed to proof) Tj
T*
(- high-value outcomes data relative to other early profiles) Tj
T*
(- enough category depth to support repeatable GTM, not just one flagship account) Tj
T*
(- attractive enough ACV to matter without requiring infrastructure-grade procurement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Indicative economics:) Tj
T*
(- likely ACV: `$250K-$750K`) Tj
T*
(- top strategic accounts: `$750K-$1.5M+`) Tj
T*
(- rough TAM: `$50M-$105M`) Tj
T*
(- rough SAM: `$20M-$40M`) Tj
T*
(- rough SOM: `$5M-$12M`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Likely decision makers:) Tj
T*
(- CEO) Tj
T*
(- COO) Tj
T*
(- CRO) Tj
T*
(- GM of enterprise / workforce solutions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Likely internal champions:) Tj
T*
(- head of strategy) Tj
T*
(- head of talent transformation) Tj
T*
(- platform/product lead for workforce intelligence or matching) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Second Move: Employer-connected mission / workforce intermediaries) Tj
T*
(Why second:) Tj
T*
(- strongest bridge from early proof into broader employer-facing and workforce-system) Tj
T*
(legitimacy) Tj
T*
(- supports a more expansive narrative around mobility, pathways, and workforce outcomes) Tj
T*
(- preserves some of the intermediary logic while broadening the market story) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Indicative economics:) Tj
T*
(- likely ACV: `$200K-$500K`) Tj
T*
(- top strategic accounts: `$500K-$1M`) Tj
T*
(- rough TAM: `$18M-$45M`) Tj
ET
endstream
